{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5","id":1512578,"title":"Ghost Council Tribe Preview for W5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-24T08:35:05-07:00","id":1512578,"title":"Ghost Council Tribe Preview for W5","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1428\" height=\"908\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/TSVG1vH.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/TSVG1vH.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/TSVG1vH.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> Some thoughts:<ul><li>The main-thing I first thought reading it was wondering yet again how a Garou-Nation ever existed in the first place when these Tribes are this divisive.</li> <li>The whole &quot;ends justify the means&quot;-approach to secrets and taboos was pushed <i>really </i>hard, I felt. At some point, I started to wonder if really taboo ideas like &quot;Maybe the Wyrm isn't as bad as Garou think...?&quot; would come up. That's the vibe I got at least.</li> <li>The Favor is written in a style more similar to the Glass-Walker-one but with three Skills instead of two and all based on a specific situation (the Hart Warden Favor is still the best one of the three).</li> <li>Again with a heavy focus on humans with archetypes and the write-ups didn't really convey that they're Garou with Garou-specific beliefs. They felt more like humans who happen to be part of the whole Garou-thing.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T08:41:02-07:00","id":1512579,"title":"","content":"Okay, at this point I'm 100% certain WW5 simply uses some leftover art from Vampire that didn't made it in to the books &gt;.&lt;<br /> This is only my humble opinion, but this is horrible<br /> Great Uktena weeps bitter tears<br /> Even the OG Ahriman with Spiritus were more Garou than these guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T08:48:59-07:00","id":1512580,"title":"","content":"Well first of all, once more the &quot;Garou cannot be with humanity much&quot; is ignored entirely. The monk here lives in a monastery and the implication is that they keep on killing their fellow monks in a never-ending cycle of penance. Interesting idea, but monasteries aren't closed off like they used to be in medieval times (barely even THEN) and deaths of fellow brothers would get the monk kicked out.<br /> <br /> The Shepherd NEEDS better art, they are the only native character shown/outright stated to be one and THEY are the ones covered in blood. I feel the blood should have been on the monk rather than on the shepherd.<br /> <br /> EDIT: But, to the preview's credit, this is a MUCH better group of example concepts than GWs and Hart Wardens had. These guys aren't defined by their jobs and have actual plot points to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 05-24-2023, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T08:57:43-07:00","id":1512583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512580#post1512580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well first of all, once more the &quot;Garou cannot be with humanity much&quot; is ignored entirely. The monk here lives in a monastery and the implication is that they keep on killing their fellow monks in a never-ending cycle of penance. Interesting idea, but monasteries aren't closed off like they used to be in medieval times (barely even THEN) and deaths of fellow brothers would get the monk kicked out.<br /> <br /> The Shepherd NEEDS better art, they are the only native character shown/outright stated to be one and THEY are the ones covered in blood. I feel the blood should have been on the monk rather than on the shepherd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the Monk and the Shepherd feel a bit out of place or in this case &quot;out of time&quot;. The Shepherd-bit mentions &quot;the Shepherd watched as, bit by bit, their ancestral lands were annexed by human governments and their customs were forced into obscurity.\u200b&quot; which is... weird. How is that even possible? Garou aren't immortal. And which region with reindeer has been annexed by a &quot;human government&quot; in the 21st century...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T09:04:40-07:00","id":1512586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512583#post1512583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both the Monk and the Shepherd feel a bit out of place or in this case &quot;out of time&quot;. The Shepherd-bit mentions &quot;the Shepherd watched as, bit by bit, their ancestral lands were annexed by human governments and their customs were forced into obscurity.\u200b&quot; which is... weird. How is that even possible? Garou aren't immortal. And which region with reindeer has been annexed by a &quot;human government&quot; in the 21st century...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lapland here in North Europe. Though it isn't officially being annexed, there are a bunch of foreign and domestic companies who are pushing to build mines and such there and the Sami and their ways are treated as a curiosity. Add to this Siberian tribes and I can totally see where the Shepherd is coming from.<br /> <br /> Plus, I live close to the capital and -I- have seen local nature being slowly but surely removed bit by bit over the years. Nevermind the tourists trap that Lapland has become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T09:09:58-07:00","id":1512587,"title":"","content":"Geez... this tribe seems a patchwork tribe from Legacy in a very unappealing way. It looks to me a bit of Shadow Lord, Striders (they had changed the &quot;Travel&quot; verb for the &quot;Seek&quot; verb on the Hart Warden website update post, but uploaded an older page into the PDF as it seems) and Stargazers... I guess because they won't be playable at all? Who knows...<br /> <br /> This tribe seems bland AF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T09:19:52-07:00","id":1512591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512586#post1512586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lapland here in North Europe. Though it isn't officially being annexed, there are a bunch of foreign and domestic companies who are pushing to build mines and such there and the Sami and their ways are treated as a curiosity. Add to this Siberian tribes and I can totally see where the Shepherd is coming from.<br /> <br /> Plus, I live close to the capital and -I- have seen local nature being slowly but surely removed bit by bit over the years. Nevermind the tourists trap that Lapland has become.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the framing just makes me think more of the 19th to 20th century. These days the issue is more about &quot;There's little left and even that is now under threat.&quot;. Like the Standing Rock protests over the pipeline or as you mentioned Lapland. Indigenous minorities have already been pushed into a tiny corner (in many regards) and now even that comes under threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T09:34:25-07:00","id":1512592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512591#post1512591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the framing just makes me think more of the 19th to 20th century. These days the issue is more about &quot;There's little left and even that is now under threat.&quot;. Like the Standing Rock protests over the pipeline or as you mentioned Lapland. Indigenous minorities have already been pushed into a tiny corner (in many regards) and now even that comes under threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the Monk DEF. sounds better in a medieval campaign.<br /> <br /> But I'd say the Shepherd as a concept is valid, as this is an issue that fits the garou AND is something that is a real issue where being a wolf-monster makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T09:44:42-07:00","id":1512594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512592#post1512592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the Monk DEF. sounds better in a medieval campaign.<br /> <br /> But I'd say the Shepherd as a concept is valid, as this is an issue that fits the garou AND is something that is a real issue where being a wolf-monster makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, all that bugs me about the Shepherd is the idea that he &quot;watched&quot; as in him being a direct witness to these events. But depending on the indigenous people the abuse they suffered happened centuries ago and continued happening for centuries. It should simply be reframed as the archetype being aware of the history and so he's invested in defending what little is left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T09:54:24-07:00","id":1512595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512594#post1512594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, all that bugs me about the Shepherd is the idea that he &quot;watched&quot; as in him being a direct witness to these events. But depending on the indigenous people the abuse they suffered happened centuries ago and continued happening for centuries. It should simply be reframed as the archetype being aware of the history and so he's invested in defending what little is left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I can buy that he watched the ways of his people go. I'm by no means indigenous, but I have watched a lot of the cultural heritage of my country go by the wayside and more global things be adopted instead. I'm in my mid-30s, and when I was a kid our Easters involved witches heavily, we had no Halloween and every new year we predicted the future from melted tin. Now easter is mostly bunnies and chicks, Halloween is a big thing and tin is no longer melted.<br /> <br /> And I'm an upper-middle-class white person, imagine those who already are on the ropes. The more global the nordic countries became, the easier it has been to lose unique aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T10:09:14-07:00","id":1512597,"title":"","content":"Is that <a href=\"https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Franz\" target=\"_blank\">Maria Franz from Heilung</a> on the left? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Her stage costume with the red dreads, antlers, and veiled eyes is a pretty distinctive look. A cute little homage, if true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T10:12:44-07:00","id":1512598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512597#post1512597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that <a href=\"https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Franz\" target=\"_blank\">Maria Franz from Heilung</a> on the left? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Her stage costume with the red dreads, antlers, and veiled eyes is a pretty distinctive look. A cute little homage, if true.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's a homage to the same culture Heilung draws inspiration from, but it is not Maria herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-24-2023, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T10:28:45-07:00","id":1512599,"title":"","content":"Huh, the artist must like the band Heilung. The left most figure is almost certainly based off of Maria Franz's hair and headress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T10:31:56-07:00","id":1512600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512599#post1512599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, the artist must like the band Heilung. The left most figure is almost certainly based off of Maria Franz's hair and headress.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's a surprisingly common costume if you look it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T10:56:58-07:00","id":1512602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512600#post1512600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it's a surprisingly common costume if you look it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to give the context, the distinctive headdress and antlers go back to a piece of artwork that tries to reconstruct a prominent grave find from the Mesolithic (the <a href=\"https://www.landesmuseum-vorgeschichte.de/en/permanent-exhibition/human-succession/the-shaman-from-bad-duerrenberg.html\" target=\"_blank\">Shaman of Bad D\u00fcrrenberg</a>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T11:02:58-07:00","id":1512603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512599#post1512599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, the artist must like the band Heilung. The left most figure is almost certainly based off of Maria Franz's hair and headress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely not a good look after the issue with the Glass Walkers art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T11:23:37-07:00","id":1512605,"title":"","content":"So James Sambrano (who previously commented on his terrible time with the first iteration with W5) commented on Twitter about the Ghost Council preview. He talked about the likeness between one picture and the singer of the group Heilung. But what I found more curious and seems very troubling is something else he previously brought up as well: That elements from the first iteration of W5 have been copy-pasted into this second iteration and the question is if the original writers will be credited.<br /> <br /> James F. Sambrano said <a href=\"https://twitter.com/indigedroid/status/1661428586069512199\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> in regards to that:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ghost Council was the name I came up with. I already knew that would appear.<br /> <br /> There two sentences and one paragraph that appear here that look almost like mine with some minor editing.<br /> <br /> There's a few that could be if you imagined heavier editing.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T12:01:10-07:00","id":1512610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512605#post1512605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So James Sambrano (who previously commented on his terrible time with the first iteration with W5) commented on Twitter about the Ghost Council preview. He talked about the likeness between one picture and the singer of the group Heilung. But what I found more curious and seems very troubling is something else he previously brought up as well: That elements from the first iteration of W5 have been copy-pasted into this second iteration and the question is if the original writers will be credited.<br /> <br /> James F. Sambrano said <a href=\"https://twitter.com/indigedroid/status/1661428586069512199\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> in regards to that:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it isn't subtle either. Yet another hed pasteded on yey work. I'm trying to see if the monk is also taken from somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T12:04:52-07:00","id":1512611,"title":"","content":"Ha! I knew I wasn't just imagining it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T12:13:32-07:00","id":1512612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512610#post1512610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it isn't subtle either. Yet another hed pasteded on yey work. I'm trying to see if the monk is also taken from somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking as well and of course, this is pure speculation... You know how you brought up that description of how Garou can't hold a job and don't work really well with humans at one point in the preview clashes with some other portrayals we got elsewhere...? What if that's the result of the writers rushing to finish the book after last October by bringing in material from the first iteration of W5? So, the reason we get two different portrayals of Garou in some sections is that this book contains writing from two different writer-teams with two different visions of what W5 is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T12:23:49-07:00","id":1512616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512612#post1512612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been thinking as well and of course, this is pure speculation... You know how you brought up that description of how Garou can't hold a job and don't work really well with humans at one point in the preview clashes with some other portrayals we got elsewhere...? What if that's the result of the writers rushing to finish the book after last October by bringing in material from the first iteration of W5? So, the reason we get two different portrayals of Garou in some sections is that this book contains writing from two different writer-teams with two different visions of what W5 is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is most likely the case in my mind as well, since we were told ONE vision by JA, then we get this current one. It feels like W5 has gone through some massive development hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T12:24:27-07:00","id":1512617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenixpp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512587#post1512587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geez... this tribe seems a patchwork tribe from Legacy in a very unappealing way. It looks to me a bit of Shadow Lord, Striders (they had changed the &quot;Travel&quot; verb for the &quot;Seek&quot; verb on the Hart Warden website update post, but uploaded an older page into the PDF as it seems) and Stargazers... I guess because they won't be playable at all? Who knows...<br /> <br /> This tribe seems bland AF.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so it's not just me, then.<br /> <br /> Seems like every writeup just hammers home a bit more that the tribes are pretty much lost without being cast as a coherent military structure. The Fera likely fair even worse (I'm still bracing for something way too close to The Hosts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T15:37:16-07:00","id":1512643,"title":"","content":"It's not really like they're making the same mistake again... it's just the one mistake is extremely pervasive. W5 basically got hit with the same problem HtV 1e did, but without the excuse of having no time to fix it after fans spotted it. Paradox should either be scrambling to scrub this artist's work from the book and get new stuff ASAP to just be safe, but we're going to just keep getting these things dribble in view the previews and they're going to fix the most egregious likeness copies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T15:51:36-07:00","id":1512648,"title":"","content":"The thing with the art is that the reason there was this delay in reaction with the GW-preview-image was that according to Outstar they managed to talk to the people who are printing the books in time. This means things were already at that advanced stage back when that controversy happened. Seems like Paradox <i>really </i>wants a physical release at Gen-Con.<br /> <br /> Now though...? There are only two options: Scrap the whole thing despite how close to a release it is or just... keep going. My bet it's the former. Of course, once the GW-problem with the image came up, there was always the question of how big of a problem we're talking about here: Is it just this one image or are there more problems lurking in the rest of the art once the public sees it...? Well, with this preview and knowing that there are 11 sets of these kinds of images... We all can do the math in our heads on how many images for these archetypes are likely based on real people and/or Google image-search results...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T16:03:11-07:00","id":1512650,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I understand correctly, but they seem to be a tribe made up of Ragabash from the SL, just without the auspice sense of humor, a dash of Tremere on the part of the research type, and the habit of traveling only more like Ravnos than what with Silent Striders, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T16:05:59-07:00","id":1512651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512648#post1512648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with the art is that the reason there was this delay in reaction with the GW-preview-image was that according to Outstar they managed to talk to the people who are printing the books in time. This means things were already at that advanced stage back when that controversy happened. Seems like Paradox <i>really </i>wants a physical release at Gen-Con.<br /> <br /> Now though...? There are only two options: Scrap the whole thing despite how close to a release it is or just... keep going. My bet it's the former. Of course, once the GW-problem with the image came up, there was always the question of how big of a problem we're talking about here: Is it just this one image or are there more problems lurking in the rest of the art once the public sees it...? Well, with this preview and knowing that there are 11 sets of these kinds of images... We all can do the math in our heads on how many images for these archetypes are likely based on real people and/or Google image-search results...</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be being biased, but many of these images would look better on Kindreds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T16:22:53-07:00","id":1512653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512650#post1512650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I understand correctly, but they seem to be a tribe made up of Ragabash from the SL, just without the auspice sense of humor, a dash of Tremere on the part of the research type, and the habit of traveling only more like Ravnos than what with Silent Striders, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, this will only get more confusing in the context of the Silent Strider write-up, I bet. After all, we know what the first paragraph says for each of these Tribes because of the cards from the Retaliation board-game and the W5 version of Silent Striders is all about exploring the Umbra. So that part of this preview confused me a bit as well. None of the Tribes so far seemed compelling, they all give off that first-draft-vibe of an idea that needs to be refined and refocused in order to become compelling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I may be being biased, but many of these images would look better on Kindreds. </div> </div> </div>Hey, according to the previews, just hanging out in the counterculture-scene and being really into the nightlife of a place is totally in line with being a W5 Garou-Pack <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> But the issue with the WtA-flavor not really coming through with these previews has been an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T17:25:53-07:00","id":1512658,"title":"","content":"I mean, I feel like at some point I'll get sick of saying this? But W5 can't handle 11 Tribes. I was of the opinion that WtA had too many Tribes as it was, and only the cultural links could really make so many of them functional as game elements.<br /> <br /> If Tribes are going to move from cultures to archetypes, they need to be archetypal.... that's not what we're seeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T17:38:41-07:00","id":1512660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512658#post1512658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I feel like at some point I'll get sick of saying this? But W5 can't handle 11 Tribes. I was of the opinion that WtA had too many Tribes as it was, and only the cultural links could really make so many of them functional as game elements.<br /> <br /> If Tribes are going to move from cultures to archetypes, they need to be archetypal.... that's not what we're seeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what specificaly are we seeing? Fan-clubs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T17:55:56-07:00","id":1512662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512660#post1512660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what specificaly are we seeing? Fan-clubs?</div> </div> </div> </div>half-baked souffles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T18:18:59-07:00","id":1512663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512610#post1512610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it isn't subtle either. Yet another hed pasteded on yey work. I'm trying to see if the monk is also taken from somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pry gonna get told to leave this thread like with the Glass Walkers, but I'll repeat that there's no excuse for lazy artist who just copy/paste existing material, give it a slight modification and then pass it off as their own. It's a bad look for the publisher when this garbage gets to print.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T20:45:09-07:00","id":1512675,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that jawline, ear and neck..not to mention hair, jewellry, headress etc. is 100% Maria Franz. Wouldn't surprise me if every human figure done by this artist is copied from an online photo....its just the other subjects aren't famous enough to have been picked up yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T21:26:07-07:00","id":1512680,"title":"","content":"They hollowed out Older Brothers corpse and replaced the innards with.....nothing?<br /> <br /> A win for cultural erasure....I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T21:56:48-07:00","id":1512684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512662#post1512662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> half-baked souffles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that an American force of speech or are you being sarcastic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T22:06:04-07:00","id":1512685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512680#post1512680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They hollowed out Older Brothers corpse and replaced the innards with.....nothing?<br /> <br /> A win for cultural erasure....I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> pretty much yeah, the one that really bothers me is the loss of wendigo/younger brother since were losing an representation of first nation canadians which as a brit, is sonething i dont really see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T22:40:32-07:00","id":1512687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512684#post1512684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that an American force of speech or are you being sarcastic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by force of speech, but anyways, it's a metaphor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T23:05:50-07:00","id":1512688,"title":"","content":"I've been silently watching the previews and I have some of my own conclusions:<br /> <br /> 1. It's a new start. It's not the Werewolf the Apocalypse. It is not a Forsaken too, but strange game about werewolves drawing from both, being something copmpletly new.<br /> 2.If 1. theory is true, I don't have any expectations about the game and so I cut off the memory of past editions, they are diiferent games in different WoD.<br /> 3. If 1 and 2 is correct, I don't make any expectations about cultural ties to tribes, cause it seems that they are based on ideas not cultures.<br /> 4. If all above is ok for me, I don't have any expectations about art.<br /> <br /> And so I buy for now what I see, reading it as if I wouldn't have any experience with WoD searching for interesting things for me, and so far I found some. So I've bought the game and even have idea to run it as shard world in umbra in my W20 campaign, <br /> <br /> That is the most healthy approach for me, I'm 40 with health problems and so I have to be as far from emotional aproach as I can.<br /> <br /> What is annoying that many shouted that Wendigo and Uktena are not represented well in WoD, so the company remade them and yeah, there are voices that the it's again messed. Golden rule - something is not good for you, change it, but yeah again people are lazy and they want everything handed them on a platter.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling that I'm buying shit in golden paper, but as I wrote I found some interesting things there. For example concept of monk/priest werewolf from Ghost Council is very good in my opinion, it's a secretive character , maby a modern hermit, holy men in local inhabitants view (and still in some places in central and western Europe You'll find them), maby local legend. Tribe have something from Bone Shadows, something from Uktena, something reckless - do your job first, consequences later. I like it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T01:25:06-07:00","id":1512694,"title":"","content":"So... An entire tribe of cringe theurges doing their best to act sigma? As for the pictures, 3/4 look like larpers.<br /> <br /> My expectations for W5 are so low I don't even think i'll borrow the book to sate a curiosity. I don't have the curiosity, it's dead. At least with V5 I can get angry, here I feel nothing but contempt. Out of three tribe previews, we have three vapid failures. It's not spicy bullshit like V5, it's just fuckin boring. At this rate I'm reckon even easy, relatively easy tribes to characterize like the Shadow Lords or Children of Gaia will be insipid word-count wastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T01:49:29-07:00","id":1512696,"title":"","content":"With the art issue, I need to be frank; This is NOT about using references. References are fine and help an artist a LOT. If the artist had used Heilung's promo art as a reference, no one would care.<br /> <br /> It is the fact that we already went through this with the GW preview and that people on the spot could say &quot;hey wait a minute&quot; about it. Unless hired to depict the target specifically, similarities like this are not a good thing.<br /> <br /> As for the tribe itself, I feel it is hurt by the removal of one of its core motives. Without trying to give the people hurt by the Wyrmcomers a voice and instead being about travel and seeking, the Ghost Council sounds like a weird Silent Strider copy. Which does not bode well for the Striders.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms said, having 11 tribes to make into the same global generalist tribes as the Forsaken tribes are is not a good idea. Each tribe of the moon and pure held one specific niche that concepts could be drawn from. Especially as the two tribes removed from the pool were one of the stronger cases of unique concepts, the Fenrir being the War tribe and the Stargazers being a fully ascetic tribe of contemplation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T02:03:02-07:00","id":1512697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512696#post1512696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the tribe itself, I feel it is hurt by the removal of one of its core motives. Without trying to give the people hurt by the Wyrmcomers a voice and instead being about travel and seeking, the Ghost Council sounds like a weird Silent Strider copy. Which does not bode well for the Striders.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms said, having 11 tribes to make into the same global generalist tribes as the Forsaken tribes are is not a good idea. Each tribe of the moon and pure held one specific niche that concepts could be drawn from. Especially as the two tribes removed from the pool were one of the stronger cases of unique concepts, the Fenrir being the War tribe and the Stargazers being a fully ascetic tribe of contemplation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree in 100%. It is not WtA but a new game cause too many things are removed/ taken away/replaced that WtA isn't what it was anymore. That's the reason I treat W5 as something different without ties to Werewolf I know. The name of the fgame and the same name for tribes stayed and it's the main similarity. There are only few left.<br /> <br /> Ripping out cultures tied to tribes, mixing and changing them removed the core from them, removed base that build the tribes in former editions. What's worse they mixed them a lot, borrowing things from one tribe and mixing with the other.<br /> <br /> What's stunned me that they merged WtF and WtA in some themes, as I am reading the previews, So ... no expectatons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T02:12:29-07:00","id":1512698,"title":"","content":"Like, if you take the description of this Tribe as &quot;seekers of mystery&quot; and having a hunger for information (of any kind) which leads them to explore stuff and look for secrets, then... how is that supposed to be distinct when you look at the W5 descriptions of Silent Striders and Bone Gnawers in this version...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Silent Striders:<br /> Masters of discovering hidden ways, the Silent Striders find themselves uniquely suited in finding their way back out again after having accomplished what they set out to do. Why not explore first and find out the best way, rather than the most direct? At worst, one may confirm another way not to undertake things. At best, one has discovered a way to get what one needs without anyone being any the wiser to the Silent Striders having been there.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers:<br /> The Bone Gnawers seek to discover the obscured in all its forms: secrets, passwords, shortcuts, anything they might use to advantage over the obvious. They are especially adept at hiding in plain sight and are often found among lower socioeconomic groups, those who go unseen by people who consider themselves superior and are careless about what their \u201clesser\u201d think or witness. </div> </div> </div>When it comes to &quot;looking for secrets&quot; as an attribute you essentially have three Tribes that all have the same MO.<br /> <br /> It would even have helped a little bit to limit the Ghost Council to being interested in spiritual secrets exclusively to at least give it some specificity. But no, stuff like investigating people and their secrets is included as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T07:55:21-07:00","id":1512735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512694#post1512694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... An entire tribe of cringe theurges doing their best to act sigma? As for the pictures, 3/4 look like larpers.<br /> <br /> My expectations for W5 are so low I don't even think i'll borrow the book to sate a curiosity. I don't have the curiosity, it's dead. At least with V5 I can get angry, here I feel nothing but contempt. Out of three tribe previews, we have three vapid failures. It's not spicy bullshit like V5, it's just fuckin boring. At this rate I'm reckon even easy, relatively easy tribes to characterize like the Shadow Lords or Children of Gaia will be insipid word-count wastes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> whatever issues v5 has is more to do with execution than anything. For example a fragmented tremere could be a great plot arc with the right angle, it's just the execution is bad. In contrast w5 is the opposite of having ideas in that it's shedding concepts and replacing them with nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-25-2023, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T15:25:33-07:00","id":1512779,"title":"","content":"Hell, the image appropriation streak keeps on giving <a href=\"https://twitter.com/The_Toering/status/1661833639145906201\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/The_Toering/stat...33639145906201</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T15:49:20-07:00","id":1512784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512675#post1512675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that jawline, ear and neck..not to mention hair, jewellry, headress etc. is 100% Maria Franz. Wouldn't surprise me if every human figure done by this artist is copied from an online photo....it\u2019s just the other subjects aren't famous enough to have been picked up yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>After seeing this, I can\u2019t say the hair is the same as Maria.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ellyawn/status/1661663969059172352?s=61&amp;t=hxkMkkgJzKwyLC60noc0hg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ellyawn/status/1661663969059172352?s=61&amp;t=hxkMkkgJzKwyLC60noc0hg\" target=\"_blank\"> Post Not Found - X | 404 Error </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ellyawn/status/1661663969059172352?s=61&amp;t=hxkMkkgJzKwyLC60noc0hg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/ellyawn/status/1661663969059172352?s=61&amp;t=hxkMkkgJzKwyLC60noc0hg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The post you're looking for could not be found or may have been deleted. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T17:25:46-07:00","id":1512799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512784#post1512784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After seeing this, I can\u2019t say the hair is the same as Maria.<br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ellyawn/status/1661663969059172352?s=61&amp;t=hxkMkkgJzKwyLC60noc0hg\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/ellyawn/status/1...zKwyLC60noc0hg</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I thought he'd just thickened and faded the braids but nope...mashed two real people together is worse.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure if turning a real Mongolian man into a faux-Saami guy is better or worse.<br /> <br /> Didn't this guy get the job because he knew Outstar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T17:34:25-07:00","id":1512800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/609799022873673729/1111449485160239184/W5-GhostCouncil1.gif\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/609799022873673729/1111449485160239184/W5-GhostCouncil1.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/609799022873673729/1111449485160239184/W5-GhostCouncil1.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/609799022873673729/1111449485160239184/W5-GhostCouncil1.gif </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T17:58:51-07:00","id":1512803,"title":"","content":"So uh, wow. Just... wow.<br /> <br /> It is a GOOD thing we have people who can track those 'references' down.<br /> <br /> The fact that there are two (noticed) of these in the Ghost Council page and one guy got race bended on top of everything is just... cherry on top of this shit sundae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T18:02:52-07:00","id":1512804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512799#post1512799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026Didn't this guy get the job because he knew Outstar?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know about that. I\u2019ll I\u2019ve seen is unsubstantiated claims of it on the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T20:00:00-07:00","id":1512807,"title":"","content":"Wow... The more I see and hear about 5E, the more I'm convinced that the whole edition outside of OPP's work and some of the fan stuff, is an incoherent, hastily put together mess. And that the 5E WoD as a whole is going to at best be held back from it could be, at worst suffer and possibly outright kill it as they continue to stumble around blindly.<br /> <br /> Honestly this is starting to get <u><i><b>PAINFUL</b></i></u> to watch. While I wasn't entirely crazy about V5 when it dropped and I've talked about my issues with that before, I was still kind of optimistic about the edition. OPP's V5 was great and proof that the in the right hands, 5E could be great. But ever since the switch off to Renegade and the SI and Sabbat books, it's been nothing but overpriced, undercooked disappointments. H5 removing the Imbued frustrated me and then hearing about how all over the place the final product was even worse. W5 is likewise shaping up to be H5 again but with traced/stolen artwork, something I didn't expect to see again after Exalted 3E. <br /> <br /> At this point I have no confidence in any official 5E WoD product that isn't from OPP and I am actively dreading M5 and Wr5 if we get them one day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T20:48:48-07:00","id":1512817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512800#post1512800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/609799022873673729/1111449485160239184/W5-GhostCouncil1.gif\" target=\"_blank\">https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachmen...stCouncil1.gif</a><br /> <br /> Yeah........</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Glass Walker's debacle, Liam Stevens said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let me be blunt here; World of Darkness is fortunate that their cultural incompetence was caught in a pre-publishing preview. Had any other page in their book been the subject of this preview, it is highly likely that this appropriation of T\u0101me\u2019s likeness and our cultural traditions would have been published. And I do wonder what other wrongs exist in the pages yet unseen. </div> </div> </div>Well now we've seen two previews and in both of them the artist has been caught appropriating other people's likeness. At this point I wouldn't be surprised if every single Tribal picture contains people that the artist has appropriated. That blatant level of appropriation of someone else's art and likeness is not acceptable at all. I don't know if the artist has been shitcanned or not, but I hope the publisher goes in and removes all of that artist's artwork before publication because it's safe to say that there will definitely be more massive, glaring issues and it's better to fix them now than to publish it and try to play defense afterward.<br /> <br /> I'm worried though that they're so intent on getting the physical release for Gencon that they won't take the time to hunt down, scrub and replacea of the problematic artwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-26-2023, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T23:15:34-07:00","id":1512826,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> WTF is this? How a proffesional artist could go THAT easy!. How? I understand inspiration, but this seems to be 1:1 picture copy with some elements added. Why they just didn't hired artists that created art in othe editions that was good, Steve Prescott or Ron Spencer for example. They try to put photo like art BUT it doesn't fit everywhere. It would even be funny but ... it just isn't. In what light does it put them in front of potential buyers. The other art previewed is very good, like cover or introdution, they could follow the concept. Ehhh shit in golden paper.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T23:52:52-07:00","id":1512827,"title":"","content":"Whisper is the folks in charge hated Spencer's artwork.....yeah.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T00:04:10-07:00","id":1512830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512817#post1512817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm worried though that they're so intent on getting the physical release for Gencon that they won't take the time to hunt down, scrub and replacea of the problematic artwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the nasty feeling they aren't going to change the art since we have ONLY seen 3/11 of the tribes and already 2/3 have suspect art noticed. There is simply too much art and too little time to get new art done.<br /> <br /> If they were smart, they'd cancel the gen-con release and go over the art VERY carefully.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T00:16:07-07:00","id":1512832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512817#post1512817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm worried though that they're so intent on getting the physical release for Gencon that they won't take the time to hunt down, scrub and replacea of the problematic artwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have to push through or cancel this book entirely which will cost them. On her WOD-news-show in the week after the whole GW-preview-debacle happened, Outstar talked about how they had to replace the art and the reason is that they had to talk to the printing company on this. So things were already at that stage at that time. So now it's pretty much unimaginable, I'd say, they could go back and change an image here or there.<br /> <br /> And they're definitely going for a physical release at GenCon. After all, the store-page has had this line added a couple of weeks ago:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Going to Gen Con and want to pick up your copy early? Use code ... at checkout. </div> </div> </div>Of course, now that we know the artist's love for tracing... Maybe for the art director as one person, it would be hard to find all the photo-references for the art used but the internet at large will solve this in no time. So when the book comes out this could cause further controversy very easily. After all, there are eleven (!) sets of people drawn by this artist in the book.<br /> <br /> And BTW, the cover-art is also from the same artist, so I'm wondering if the factory we see on the cover also involved tracing. Maybe it's a photo of a steel-mill or something that was used as a reference there...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T02:11:58-07:00","id":1512841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512827#post1512827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whisper is the folks in charge hated Spencer's artwork.....yeah.....</div> </div> </div> </div>thats an....interesting mindset. Spencer isn't to my taste but I'd take it over the mediocrity incarnate of 5th ed art and that's before we consider the endless gaffes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T03:11:34-07:00","id":1512850,"title":"","content":"It's remarkable how much good will has been evaporated. Some with bad output, some with contempt.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering what the spin will be, if W5 ends up bombing. &quot;The old fans were Too Racist&quot; might have some legs; on twitter there was a solid week where anyone saying they didn't like Eternals was presented as having been put off by the diverse cast, and not the film being awful.<br /> <br /> My first news of this preview was a GIF showing the Shepherd preview turning into a real-life guy. Again. STOP MANIPULATING PHOTOGRAPHS OF REAL PEOPLE!<br /> <br /> Anyways looking at the tribal art for W20 is so refreshing after these previews. They're in a variety of the three Breed Forms, they are in a cool comic book art style, and you can identify the Tribe's identity and vibe INSTANTLY by looking at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T03:44:36-07:00","id":1512851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512850#post1512850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My first news of this preview was a GIF showing the Shepherd preview turning into a real-life guy. Again. STOP MANIPULATING PHOTOGRAPHS OF REAL PEOPLE!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel I must note something; You should not manipulate images of real people <b>that you have no permission of using.</b> Stock images exist for a reason, even if it is looked at a bit askew in art circles to trace from them. Heck, there are 3D programs with free realistic human models to trace from. Or you could take your own photographs. There are plenty of non-stealy options.<br /> <br /> The issue with this fellow is twofold; First of all, these are straight traces with very minor edits of people with fame. Second, this edition is supposed to be the non-racist one, yet we have race bending in this preview. Nevermind the GW one.<br /> <br /> And as you said, they could have chosen to go a more comic-book way and this would not have happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T04:07:23-07:00","id":1512853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512832#post1512832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, now that we know the artist's love for tracing... Maybe for the art director as one person, it would be hard to find all the photo-references for the art used but the internet at large will solve this in no time. So when the book comes out this could cause further controversy very easily. After all, there are eleven (!) sets of people drawn by this artist in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that when the book releases, within hours you'll have internet detectives finding many, maybe dozens of people who had their likenesses appropriated without their permission, and I suspect that the controversy will overshadow any positive points about the game's release on social media.<br /> <br /> I hope Outstar is already polishing their apology tour because I expect this will go over like a lead balloon with most people. Tracing photographs in order to steal people's likeness and make money off of them isn't something that I see anybody approving of. This is the kind of thing that can kill a game in its early stages if it has the deserved reputation for stealing artwork or other material from people. Why would you want to support a company that does that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-26-2023, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T08:01:44-07:00","id":1512871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512850#post1512850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's remarkable how much good will has been evaporated. Some with bad output, some with contempt.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering what the spin will be, if W5 ends up bombing. &quot;The old fans were Too Racist&quot; might have some legs; on twitter there was a solid week where anyone saying they didn't like Eternals was presented as having been put off by the diverse cast, and not the film being awful.<br /> <br /> My first news of this preview was a GIF showing the Shepherd preview turning into a real-life guy. Again. STOP MANIPULATING PHOTOGRAPHS OF REAL PEOPLE!<br /> <br /> Anyways looking at the tribal art for W20 is so refreshing after these previews. They're in a variety of the three Breed Forms, they are in a cool comic book art style, and you can identify the Tribe's identity and vibe INSTANTLY by looking at them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> its been a slow erosion. The tacit disdain and laziness of most products and protective antipathy about the fans has taken its toll. You're talking about a company which seems to hate its fandom while trying to charge 15 bucks for a single dice.<br /> <br /> Maybe, trouble is wod fans genrally arnt racist. At worst they're culturally insensitive sometimes with a few bad eggs inevitable with a product. You also run the risk of cry wolf and the irl danger of cognitively linking socially conscious art with crap.<br /> <br /> Yeah just draw your own shit.<br /> <br /> wod has always benefited from stylised larger than life depictions rather than realistic. Look at theo Bell in v20 and revised vs his look in 5th to see my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-26-2023, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T08:04:20-07:00","id":1512872,"title":"","content":"At first I was just disappointed with the preview, and fearing what will happen to the SL - my personal favorite tribe.<br /> <br /> But those art problems are just bizarre. I was already not a fan of this &quot;Human: the Outcasts&quot; vibe before, but there's just no defense anymore. And if that doesn't kill the 5E, I'm afraid the bar will just get lower and lower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T09:27:23-07:00","id":1512881,"title":"","content":"Oh to be clear when I say &quot;might have some legs&quot; in my previous post, I don't mean in terms of being an accurate assessment, I mean in terms of convincing people online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T09:51:19-07:00","id":1512884,"title":"","content":"I really loved the art of the old editions. The black and white stuff, especially when it got twisted, weird and wyrmy. V20's style was different and i've got some reservations (Klaives are way too big, crinos forms maybe a little over-heroic, my friends and I all laughing about the legendary Lasombra side-boob) but it also had some great stuff too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ironically the one picture I really loved from V5 was the one with a werewolf slashing someone in half. You'd think werewolf'd be doing a good job here. <br /> <br /> I wanna see crinos, lupus or hispo with beautiful tribe fur, graciously ornamented with tribe-typical fetishes. Is that so much to ask?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-26-2023, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T10:04:51-07:00","id":1512888,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious about the art for the Red Talons now. Are even those four humans/weird-looking one who is in Glabro presumably...?<br /> <br /> But I think one reason we get humans for the most part is that this version of W5 the focus is on Homids and the game <i>really </i>wants you to play Homids. And I guess, maybe the artist got directions to emphasize humans. Or he just read the archetypes. I mean... none of them were wolf-born thus far, right? Even though it supposedly is still a player-option to be wolf-born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T10:40:05-07:00","id":1512891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512888#post1512888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really curious about the art for the Red Talons now. Are even those four humans/weird-looking one who is in Glabro presumably...?<br /> <br /> But I think one reason we get humans for the most part is that this version of W5 the focus is on Homids and the game <i>really </i>wants you to play Homids. And I guess, maybe the artist got directions to emphasize humans. Or he just read the archetypes. I mean... none of them were wolf-born thus far, right? Even though it supposedly is still a player-option to be wolf-born.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll probably just have pictures of extra-shaggy and unkempt people for the Talons, some of whom are wearing only deer furs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T11:03:20-07:00","id":1512893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512884#post1512884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really loved the art of the old editions. The black and white stuff, especially when it got twisted, weird and wyrmy. V20's style was different and i've got some reservations (Klaives are way too big, crinos forms maybe a little over-heroic, my friends and I all laughing about the legendary Lasombra side-boob) but it also had some great stuff too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ironically the one picture I really loved from V5 was the one with a werewolf slashing someone in half. You'd think werewolf'd be doing a good job here.<br /> <br /> I wanna see crinos, lupus or hispo with beautiful tribe fur, graciously ornamented with tribe-typical fetishes. Is that so much to ask?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One of things the classic character arts do is 'sell' the idea of the group. Lasombra side boob aside she tells you a lot about the clan is her look. Some do a really do a good job of this like w20 get of fenris. 5th ed is really bad at this even with easy slam dunks like the nosferatu lineup and werewolf seems to follow this trend, you could easily swap a lot of w5 tribe art around and it would not make a difference. For example one of them is just a slightly creepy monk another a generic soldier, neither tell us anything distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-26-2023, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T12:16:15-07:00","id":1512899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512891#post1512891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They'll probably just have pictures of extra-shaggy and unkempt people for the Talons, some of whom are wearing only deer furs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or GSDs in wolf coats, if they actually commit to the wolf bit XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T12:52:10-07:00","id":1512903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512899#post1512899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or GSDs in wolf coats, if they actually commit to the wolf bit XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Or someone traces San from Princess Mononoke. I doubt that would happen, though; it would probably give us too good of an idea of the human-born Garou that join the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-26-2023, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T13:57:30-07:00","id":1512909,"title":"","content":"Red Talons should go Naked. Since virtually all werewolves are fit it's not a bad choice. Wearing hides is humanish enough to be a negative thing for RT but simultaneously it won't let them fit in with humans much so they might as well just grab some human clothes. IDK say something like &quot;It's 100% natural materials&quot; or &quot;I killed a human and stole his clothes&quot; and it'll be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T14:24:11-07:00","id":1512911,"title":"","content":"It's not like you'd be able to tell if Red Talons in Homid are fit at a distance, given that they're unlikely to wax or shave but are likely to have a carpet of hair all around, which tends to obscure muscle mass. Unless, like, there's a Camp of the Wild Scouring that ritualistically shaves each other to achieve perfect swimwear zones.<br /> <br /> (&quot;I killed a human and took their stuff&quot; is probably the most sensible case, but since this is W5, we can't have anything like that.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T14:31:14-07:00","id":1512912,"title":"","content":"That is all assuming they just wear a bit torn clothes and matted hair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T15:33:13-07:00","id":1512918,"title":"","content":"Holy crap. The art is worse than I thought. Maria Franz's headdress pasted onto a direct trace of another woman, the &quot;reindeer herder&quot; race bending. The artist needs to be fired, blacklisted, and all art of theirs stripped from the book as suspect.<br /> <br /> My sister is an artist and I shared this with her. To quote her, &quot;With &quot;artists&quot; like this, who needs AI to rip off the rest of us?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T19:12:24-07:00","id":1512927,"title":"","content":"There's a weird part in the witch description about her worldview.<br /> <br /> &quot;Gaia is a metaphor, and so are spirits. It's all in the way the individual sees the world, which eyes they choose.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whaaaaaaat? Did you put that just to looks mystical? This is werewolf the apocalypse and she's clearly a theurge. I can accept that, in a edition where gaia is dying/dead, young garou might see her as metaphor, but spirits? They are as concrete to garou as are humans.<br /> <br /> &quot;-spirits are metaphor, it's all in the way glargblarah *wet, strangled noise as the witch has her throat cutted by the &quot;metaphorical&quot; bane*<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T21:11:16-07:00","id":1512930,"title":"","content":"Maybe they meant personification or representation? But yeah, I see a snarky Ragabash saying, &quot;Congrats. I've heard of people wrestling with metaphors before, but you're the first person to ever get their ass kicked by one.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T23:29:44-07:00","id":1512932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512927#post1512927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a weird part in the witch description about her worldview.<br /> <br /> &quot;Gaia is a metaphor, and so are spirits. It's all in the way the individual sees the world, which eyes they choose.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whaaaaaaat? Did you put that just to looks mystical? This is werewolf the apocalypse and she's clearly a theurge. I can accept that, in a edition where gaia is dying/dead, young garou might see her as metaphor, but spirits? They are as concrete to garou as are humans.<br /> <br /> &quot;-spirits are metaphor, it's all in the way glargblarah *wet, strangled noise as the witch has her throat cutted by the &quot;metaphorical&quot; bane*<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same vein, the way it ends is also weird: &quot;They are blind, whereas the Witch can see, and Witch\u2019s packmates would do well to remember the elective ignorance in which human society chooses to cloak itself.\u200b&quot; What are they talking about...? They're all Garou and one thing that does unite them is their animistic worldview that they also know is very real since they can travel through the Umbra and interact with spirits. I guess, with the mid-Apocalypse-setting you could kinda imagine young Garou running around who don't really know what's going on but the introduction we've gotten in the previews really sets it up as a &quot;truth&quot; that Garou know about spirits. Oh, and this bit also seems weird: &quot;It\u2019s not parlor tricks \u2014 the way so many charlatans try to pass off the Gift \u2014 it\u2019s a genuine relationship with the world beyond the boundary of the one most humans can perceive.\u200b&quot; I mean, &quot;charlatans try to pass off the Gift&quot;... and it's even capital-G Gift... In this context, the capital-G Gift of this splat is being a werewolf/Garou, so that's a weird way to talk about it. What it's obviously getting at is some sort of &quot;true magic vs parlor tricks&quot;-distinction but... this is WtA...<br /> <br /> The write-up just feels so weird.<br /> <br /> But the majority of the archetypes that we've seen up to this point have had this problem of either not really giving off the vibe of either being a Garou and/or a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T01:17:10-07:00","id":1512933,"title":"","content":"That Witch would\u2019ve been perfect as a rogue Kinfolk turned Awakened lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T01:25:03-07:00","id":1512934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512932#post1512932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It\u2019s not parlor tricks \u2014 the way so many charlatans try to pass off the Gift \u2014 it\u2019s a genuine relationship with the world beyond the boundary of the one most humans can perceive.\u200b&quot; I mean, &quot;charlatans try to pass off the Gift&quot;... and it's even capital-G Gift... In this context, the capital-G Gift of this splat is being a werewolf/Garou, so that's a weird way to talk about it. What it's obviously getting at is some sort of &quot;true magic vs parlor tricks&quot;-distinction but... this is WtA...<br /> <br /> The write-up just feels so weird.<br /> <br /> But the majority of the archetypes that we've seen up to this point have had this problem of either not really giving off the vibe of either being a Garou and/or a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am guessing since the focus is on humanity and existing within cities, that some garou try to pass off their gifts to humans as just sleight of hand. While the witch seems to be of the opinion that doing so is stupid and they should KNOW her powers come from the spirits.<br /> <br /> I think the best way to read these is through the lens of humanity first.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, unless a pack is mentioned, I think the best assumption is that the Archetype is the ONLY garou around/is a lone wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 05-27-2023, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T02:06:17-07:00","id":1512935,"title":"","content":"I know this has been said to death, but if they aren't defined by their Packs, and they're all born into and live in human society, and they solve problems using human methods and jobs, and none of the character writeups mention Garou society or using any form other than Homid...<br /> <br /> Why are these characters Werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T04:26:25-07:00","id":1512940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512935#post1512935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this has been said to death, but if they aren't defined by their Packs, and they're all born into and live in human society, and they solve problems using human methods and jobs, and none of the character writeups mention Garou society or using any form other than Homid...<br /> <br /> Why are these characters Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking on it, theyre not-theyre mages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T04:30:40-07:00","id":1512941,"title":"","content":"Was bored, so I googled a bit and I've found the image of the face the artist traced for the female soldier on this preview: It's the soldier in the middle of this <a href=\"https://www.timesofisrael.com/after-heading-co-ed-battalion-an-idf-officer-sees-women-soon-leading-the-charge/\" target=\"_blank\">article</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T04:49:02-07:00","id":1512943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512941#post1512941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was bored, so I googled a bit and I've found the image of the face the artist traced for the female soldier on this preview: It's the soldier in the middle of this <a href=\"https://www.timesofisrael.com/after-heading-co-ed-battalion-an-idf-officer-sees-women-soon-leading-the-charge/\" target=\"_blank\">article</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point I am absolutely positive that every single piece of work this artist has done involves uncredited tracing from googled images.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T05:02:39-07:00","id":1512944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512943#post1512943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this point I am absolutely positive that every single piece of work this artist has done involves uncredited tracing from googled images.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% Agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T05:09:07-07:00","id":1512945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512943#post1512943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this point I am absolutely positive that every single piece of work this artist has done involves uncredited tracing from googled images.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I'm right there with you. Now it's only a matter of just how bad the fallout of this will be. The worst case is someone actually drags them into court over this. But somebody whose photo has been traced just going on social media and talking about how their work has been stolen or they've been depicted without permission is already enough to create some <i>really </i>bad PR for the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T05:18:23-07:00","id":1512946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512945#post1512945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, I'm right there with you. Now it's only a matter of just how bad the fallout of this will be. The worst case is someone actually drags them into court over this. But somebody whose photo has been traced just going on social media and talking about how their work has been stolen or they've been depicted without permission is already enough to create some <i>really </i>bad PR for the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. At this point, it seems like the right move legally and ethically for Paradox to take is to pull this book from the printers entirely and remove all of this artist's work from the project before resuming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T06:51:06-07:00","id":1512950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512946#post1512946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. At this point, it seems like the right move legally and ethically for Paradox to take is to pull this book from the printers entirely and remove all of this artist's work from the project before resuming.</div> </div> </div> </div>They really should. But I'm doubtful they will as they want to get the first copies to Gencon. They don't have much time and depending on how much art this person has done, it could cause significant delays and potentially prevent that.<br /> <br /> And given how much of a growing train wreck 5E has been since they handed it off to Renegade, it wouldn't really surprise me at this point that if they just throw up their hands and ignore any further calls to replace traced/stolen artwork, caring more about getting W5 to market for Gencon.<br /> <br /> They will most likely drop the artist and never use them again but that's about the best we can hope for really. At the moment it seems that W5 will at best be Blandwolf: the Generic and at worst, will be like H5, a horrid, misshapen mixture of Apocalypse and Forsaken that misses the point of both.<br /> <br /> Frankly the only W5 thing I'm potentially looking forward to are any potential OPP products and fanworks on the Vault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T07:24:54-07:00","id":1512953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512945#post1512945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, I'm right there with you. Now it's only a matter of just how bad the fallout of this will be. The worst case is someone actually drags them into court over this. But somebody whose photo has been traced just going on social media and talking about how their work has been stolen or they've been depicted without permission is already enough to create some <i>really </i>bad PR for the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind the sources of these pictures go from photoshoots to people from IRL conflicts. Which is even WORSE.<br /> <br /> Though, since the artist IS Polish, one has to wonder about the copyright law there. Not that it matters much in a global product like W5, but if the laws there are more permissive it might explain a few things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T07:28:36-07:00","id":1512954,"title":"","content":"Any publisher would have a talk with the artist after the fallout of the GW preview whether any other artwork was traced this way. It was obvious that once released to a wider audience, it would get noticed- especially with public figures like that. The decision to go through with it was probably already made at that point.<br /> <br /> From what I read I get the feeling that in-house the product isn't exactly a passion project either, and they want to be just done with it. There is probably some strong executive pressure towards that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T07:41:19-07:00","id":1512957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512954#post1512954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any publisher would have a talk with the artist after the fallout of the GW preview whether any other artwork was traced this way. It was obvious that once released to a wider audience, it would get noticed- especially with public figures like that. The decision to go through with it was probably already made at that point.<br /> <br /> From what I read I get the feeling that in-house the product isn't exactly a passion project either, and they want to be just done with it. There is probably some strong executive pressure towards that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I've been getting that sense to. For all their faults, the early V5 stuff at least felt like it was being done by people that cared about VtM. And of course the OPP products were brimming with love for VtM and it's history. But the more recent stuff? From what I've heard and read, it feels increasingly like a soulless cash grab, banking on the name and little else. Look at H5. Despite having the HtR name, the Imbued were retconned out in favor of a mishmash of Hunters Hunted and Hunter: the Vigil despite it actually making more sense with the material in the book for them to be Imbued Hunters rather than normal Hunters. And if they truly wanted just normal Hunters in WoD, they easily could have a Hunters Hunted 5E but they wanted the name recognition of HtR so gave it that name instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T07:49:58-07:00","id":1512958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512954#post1512954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I read I get the feeling that in-house the product isn't exactly a passion project either, and they want to be just done with it. There is probably some strong executive pressure towards that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, W5 has been thrown about like a hot potato for YEARS. If I remember right, the By Night Studios book was using the first concept for W5.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T07:50:12-07:00","id":1512959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512934#post1512934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am guessing since the focus is on humanity and existing within cities, that some garou try to pass off their gifts to humans as just sleight of hand. While the witch seems to be of the opinion that doing so is stupid and they should KNOW her powers come from the spirits.<br /> <br /> I think the best way to read these is through the lens of humanity first.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, unless a pack is mentioned, I think the best assumption is that the Archetype is the ONLY garou around/is a lone wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm no native English speaker here, but when I did read the piece I got the impression that it meant that usually charlatans pass off their parlor tricks for real magic, but she can see when someone has a a real Gift, like her. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T07:51:05-07:00","id":1512960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512958#post1512958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, W5 has been thrown about like a hot potato for YEARS. If I remember right, the By Night Studios book was using the first concept for W5.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The reverse, I think Martin started developing W5 using the BNS book as a base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T11:02:23-07:00","id":1512985,"title":"","content":"V5 feels like the project of someone who read a corebook or had a few games, found it interesting enough but didn't get too deep with it and decided they wanted to change it into something perfect for their particular vision. <br /> <br /> This can work (<i>The Boys</i> show is much better than it's comic, <i>Starship Troopers</i> being better or not is a matter for debate) but it usually sucks. <br /> <br /> W5 on the otherhand feels like the project of someone who got a summary, didn't like it at all and had absolutely no interest in the project, but still pushed something out because a paycheck was needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T12:28:28-07:00","id":1512994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512985#post1512985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 feels like the project of someone who read a corebook or had a few games, found it interesting enough but didn't get too deep with it and decided they wanted to change it into something perfect for their particular vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 core is literally packed with references to earlier and obscure lore, and was designed together with the creator of the game. <br /> <br /> Of all the possible criticism that can be directed at V5, that it was done by superficial people who didn' really know the game and the lore, or maybe didn't even like it, is the most unfair, it borders on gatekeeping <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T12:41:44-07:00","id":1512995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512994#post1512994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 core is literally packed with references to earlier and obscure lore, and was designed together with the creator of the game.<br /> <br /> Of all the possible criticism that can be directed at V5, that it was done by superficial people who didn' really know the game and the lore, or maybe didn't even like it, is the most unfair, it borders on gatekeeping <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say a better way to say it was that it feels (to me) that the earlier works involved partly the work of people who loved Vampire and were invested in continuing its depth, and part of it was people who decided that everything VtM became past a narrow focus on aspects of 1e and revised was a mistake that needed undoing.<br /> Following the Players Guide, H5 and W5 we're now at the point where it definitely feels like its in the hands of people who either don't care about the original WoD or dislike it. I'm not claiming to be able to read their minds, but that's how it comes across from over here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T13:12:20-07:00","id":1512999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512994#post1512994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 core is literally packed with references to earlier and obscure lore, and was designed together with the creator of the game.<br /> <br /> Of all the possible criticism that can be directed at V5, that it was done by superficial people who didn' really know the game and the lore, or maybe didn't even like it, is the most unfair, it borders on gatekeeping <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's entirely possible to include and utilize a lot of details without really understanding the core concept. Some people can list off names and dates in history like an encyclopedia and yet entirely mischaracterise the people and customs of a period. Yes, a big character like Theo Bell did something, but no, it doesn't make sense within the context. Yes, Carna is a character from somewhere; no, that's not how the Tremere so far characterized would work in this situation. You know that wrong feeling you get when you watch disney Star Wars? They're using both big names and obscure content from comics nobody reads and yet &quot;<i>somehow, palpatine has returned&quot;</i> (I could really go into a long list of things that don't belong in Star Wars like hyperspace ramming but that's not the point) <br /> Vampire hunters would never cooperate on such a large scale, The Brujah would never leave the Cam, the Cam would never give up it's monopoly, the Lasombra would never take that deal, the Tremere are too institutionalized and paranoid to take Carna's offer, elders fucking off into some kind of weird crusade so the neonates can have their fun is utterly antithetical to the struggles of vampire, hunger dice is utterly antithetical to the idea of &quot;A Beast I am lest a Beast I become&quot;. Making Carna a big deal is like giving Mando the N1 starfighter; It's nice that you did some research but it doesn't make any fucking sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T13:24:20-07:00","id":1513002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512985#post1512985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W5 on the otherhand feels like the project of someone who got a summary, didn't like it at all and had absolutely no interest in the project, but still pushed something out because a paycheck was needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've said before, doing a different type of werewolf game would have been fine. In fact, there is a niche unfilled in WoD for cursed were-creatures.<br /> <br /> But this is barely even about werewolves at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T13:26:42-07:00","id":1513003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1512995#post1512995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say a better way to say it was that it feels (to me) that the earlier works involved partly the work of people who loved Vampire and were invested in continuing its depth, and part of it was people who decided that everything VtM became past a narrow focus on aspects of 1e and revised was a mistake that needed undoing.<br /> Following the Players Guide, H5 and W5 we're now at the point where it definitely feels like its in the hands of people who either don't care about the original WoD or dislike it. I'm not claiming to be able to read their minds, but that's how it comes across from over here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's generally believed that the idea with v5 was they intended to expand beyond the core back to basics. Unfortunately the corebook mechanics and setting are badly set up for that and the implosion of white wolf scuppered that idea anyway so we're stuck spinning our wheel at year one. Their is a difference between v5 and other 5th games in that v5 feels like a sincere effort with some fondness for the source material however. W5 seems to almost be annoyed to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-28-2023, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T16:02:12-07:00","id":1513012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513003#post1513003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It's generally believed that the idea with v5 was they intended to expand beyond the core back to basics and then expand quickly beyond that. Unfortunately the corebook mechanics and setting are badly set up for that and the implosion of white wolf scuppered that idea anyway so we're stuck spinning our wheel at year one. Their is a difference between v5 and other 5th games in that v5 feels like a sincere effort with some fondness for the source material however. W5 seems to almost be annoyed to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either annoyed to exist or annoyed at what came before and having to make even a small effort to connect to it in even the most minor way. I kind of get the impression that W5 wants to be completely divorced from what came before aside from taking some bits and mechanics from WtA and WtF. Much like H5 in that regards which frankly is a distressing sign for any future 5E lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T17:25:57-07:00","id":1513016,"title":"","content":"To me, the more distressing sign is that they still seem fine with not replacing Justin Achilli. Even if I strongly dislike his design direction for WoD5e, you need someone in charge. Paradox hasn't announced fully handing that over to Renegade either... and seem to be settling for literal design by committee using whatever notes and ideas left over from the previous brand leads as a framework. I can't imagine things are going to get better just having a WoD &quot;team&quot; at Paradox that isn't being run by people with RPG design experience making major design decisions going forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T17:44:30-07:00","id":1513017,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of Justin Achilli's decisions as lead-dev of WOD5E either but there's something that's also been bothering me... So last October when the first couple previews were talked about, when it came to a release date the phrase that JA always used was &quot;tentatively 2023&quot;. But the moment he was gone, the announcement was &quot;GenCon 2023... and we're gonna try <i>really hard</i> to make a physical release happen at that time as well!&quot;. This is also just another point in giving this release the vibe of this thing just being pushed out the door no matter what, like &quot;This thing is gonna get released in 2023 come hell or high water...&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T18:31:42-07:00","id":1513023,"title":"","content":"I've been out of the loop for a couple of days as I was on a trip, and I see we're back to photoediting.<br /> <br /> The Ghost Council itself left me quite confused. What makes them a council? Where is a structure they belong to and how do they communicate and what is their agenda? This seems to be just a name (again). I understand they're supposed to be pragmatic scholars - but what are they studying? What are these mysteries and taboos they are challenging?<br /> <br /> How does the give and take with Horned Serpent work? What is the transaction in question? Which fairy tale quality are we talking about? What's its agenda? How does this even work!? If the new tribes are truly Mystery Cults of Totems now, the key character in every Tribe should be their totem, and we get about a line or two for each and nothing is really defined about what they're actually about.<br /> <br /> In general, they've spent a large number of words over two pages repeating the same content and not actually giving anything to bite into. Give me something to latch onto, something that makes them special and explains how they slot into the setting, not just a repetition of nebulous traits!<br /> <br /> <br /> At least it's not the voice that's writing the characters, because Gaia, whoever is writing that is trying way too hard to be &quot;conversational&quot; and &quot;hip&quot;, while failing at both. Even with going past the writing, I wonder what these folks have to offer to the Garou at large? The Ascetic lives in the middle of nowhere disconnected from life making amends when it snaps, the Saboteur coopts weaver tech to blow stuff up. The Shepherd is one that could work as Garou, but there is nothing about how this interacts with packs, septs or Caerns, it's wholly defined by the ethnic conflict over their role in the broader conflict that defines the game (even in the current previews).<br /> <br /> The Witch may be the only one that's actually a investigator of the unknown and forbidden out of the four, but reading the description just makes me cringe. She sounds like a bad New Age joke rather than a believer, letalone a member of a society that belongs to the worlds of spirit and has a divine right to interacting and knowing about the secrets of the universe.<br /> <br /> I'm really not sure why I'm still doing this to myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T23:47:29-07:00","id":1513045,"title":"","content":"They have stopped announcing the previews on their twitter,too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T05:48:29-07:00","id":1513066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513023#post1513023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been out of the loop for a couple of days as I was on a trip, and I see we're back to photoediting.<br /> <br /> The Ghost Council itself left me quite confused. What makes them a council? Where is a structure they belong to and how do they communicate and what is their agenda? This seems to be just a name (again).</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that has come out is that James Sambrano who worked on the first version of the game is the person who came up with the new name Ghost Council and there's a couple of sentences and some edited passages still in this section. But that explains why the name doesn't seem to fit: The person who wrote most of this second version didn't come up with the name. No idea why the WOD-team of this second iteration decided to copy/paste stuff from the first iteration. This could also explain the give-and-take-bit with the Patron-Spirit. Maybe it's a remnant of the first version that is still here for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513023#post1513023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand they're supposed to be pragmatic scholars - but what are they studying? What are these mysteries and taboos they are challenging?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it first starts by calling them &quot;contemplatives&quot; and &quot;scholars&quot; but later on the idea of what they're after gets much broader, like &quot;learning where in his mistress\u2019 apartment the executive hid incriminating documents\u200b&quot; isn't very scholarly. So what I got from it is that in a very broad sense, they are interested in secrets and I mean again secrets here as in a very general idea of secrets. And what kind of taboos are they challenging...? I mean, all of them, it's just this general idea of ignoring taboos and crossing boundaries. Where I thought it went somewhat too far was with the &quot;ends justify the means&quot; bit leading to the line &quot;If something comes of maintaining a relationship with a confidant \u200bfrom a fallen tribe or forging pacts with forbidden spirits, the Ghost is satisfied \u2014 and validated, in their minds.\u200b&quot; So working together with BSD or Wyrm spirits is completely fine as long as it gets the Ghost closer to their goal... That's what it sounds like to me at least. You'd think this Tribe would've gotten kicked out of the Nation ages ago if they're this blas\u00e9 about taboos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T07:24:05-07:00","id":1513072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513002#post1513002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this is barely even about werewolves at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly you could do a WtA reboot that didn't focus on the werewolf aspect that much. Go hard on the eco-terrorist/shaman angle, ramp up the importance of playable Kinfolk, and really bang that 'the Garou are dying' drum.<br /> <br /> It would be like making a Star Wars game without playable Jedi, but in the same way it could work. I even personally prefer that side of Werewolf to the raging death monster and tribal meetings side. But of course at that point you might as well call it Kinfolk: the Uprising rather than Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T07:27:15-07:00","id":1513073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513072#post1513072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly you could do a WtA reboot that didn't focus on the werewolf aspect that much. Go hard on the eco-terrorist/shaman angle, ramp up the importance of playable Kinfolk, and really bang that 'the Garou are dying' drum.<br /> <br /> It would be like making a Star Wars game without playable Jedi, but in the same way it could work. I even personally prefer that side of Werewolf to the raging death monster and tribal meetings side. But of course at that point you might as well call it Kinfolk: the Uprising rather than Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>That idea is cool, but when I pick up a book called werewolves, I do want to play werewolves XD<br /> <br /> I honestly am for kinfolk games like that, because kinfolk are such a good mid-point between garou and humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T08:29:41-07:00","id":1513078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513023#post1513023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been out of the loop for a couple of days as I was on a trip, and I see we're back to photoediting.<br /> <br /> The Ghost Council itself left me quite confused. What makes them a council? Where is a structure they belong to and how do they communicate and what is their agenda? This seems to be just a name (again). I understand they're supposed to be pragmatic scholars - but what are they studying? What are these mysteries and taboos they are challenging?<br /> <br /> How does the give and take with Horned Serpent work? What is the transaction in question? Which fairy tale quality are we talking about? What's its agenda? How does this even work!? If the new tribes are truly Mystery Cults of Totems now, the key character in every Tribe should be their totem, and we get about a line or two for each and nothing is really defined about what they're actually about.<br /> <br /> In general, they've spent a large number of words over two pages repeating the same content and not actually giving anything to bite into. Give me something to latch onto, something that makes them special and explains how they slot into the setting, not just a repetition of nebulous traits!<br /> <br /> <br /> At least it's not the voice that's writing the characters, because Gaia, whoever is writing that is trying way too hard to be &quot;conversational&quot; and &quot;hip&quot;, while failing at both. Even with going past the writing, I wonder what these folks have to offer to the Garou at large? The Ascetic lives in the middle of nowhere disconnected from life making amends when it snaps, the Saboteur coopts weaver tech to blow stuff up. The Shepherd is one that could work as Garou, but there is nothing about how this interacts with packs, septs or Caerns, it's wholly defined by the ethnic conflict over their role in the broader conflict that defines the game (even in the current previews).<br /> <br /> The Witch may be the only one that's actually a investigator of the unknown and forbidden out of the four, but reading the description just makes me cringe. She sounds like a bad New Age joke rather than a believer, letalone a member of a society that belongs to the worlds of spirit and has a divine right to interacting and knowing about the secrets of the universe.<br /> <br /> I'm really not sure why I'm still doing this to myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're taking being open and vague very seriously, I mean leaving everything very open so, in theory, new players can put whatever they want in the chronicle, or if you push it too hard you can think that each of these tribes are less a divided nation and more individual groups surviving and acting according to their own agendas. At this rate, I think people will invest more in creating fan-made W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T10:39:00-07:00","id":1513091,"title":"","content":"Weird name changes. I would've gone for something more.. punchy. <br /> <br /> Fianna- Horned Hounds, (I would consider howlers were it not for the white howlers) <br /> Uktena- Bane Eaters/tenders<br /> Wendigo- Cold Jaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T13:08:56-07:00","id":1513105,"title":"","content":"pointless snark, delete pls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-28-2023, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T06:41:03-07:00","id":1513191,"title":"","content":"I've found the photo that was used for the factory on the cover of the book. It's traced from a <a href=\"https://www.shutterstock.com/de/image-photo/oil-refinery-plant-heavy-industry-estate-256914487\" target=\"_blank\">Shutterstock-photo</a>. Not the worst thing we've seen thus far but man, it really goes to show that with this artist you can count on the fact that a photo was traced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T09:44:34-07:00","id":1513201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513191#post1513191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've found the photo that was used for the factory on the cover of the book. It's traced from a <a href=\"https://www.shutterstock.com/de/image-photo/oil-refinery-plant-heavy-industry-estate-256914487\" target=\"_blank\">Shutterstock-photo</a>. Not the worst thing we've seen thus far but man, it really goes to show that with this artist you can count on the fact that a photo was traced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, every artist using a model or depicting a real-life landscape, from the Classic Age onwards, would be &quot;tracing&quot;, then: I don't think there's a lot of artists whose work only come out of their imagination, without prior reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T10:04:34-07:00","id":1513204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513201#post1513201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, every artist using a model or depicting a real-life landscape, from the Classic Age onwards, would be &quot;tracing&quot;, then: I don't think there's a lot of artists whose work only come out of their imagination, without prior reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue isn't that any artist in question shouldn't be allowed to do this. But the process we're talking about here is taking photos that somebody else took, put online and then tracing them for your own art-project. With stock-photos the process is, of course, a lot easier, but if you're taking somebody else's creative work in the form of photography and it's heavily referenced, the artist should at least mention the reference or once we get past stock-photos have to ask for permission first and/or recompense the original model/photograph whose photo was used. Especially once we start talking about art in a product that's being sold. The GW-preview-debacle happened because this wasn't taken seriously. Some guy's face was traced and the art-work was put into the book. But it turns out... there should be a little more to this process because otherwise, you end up creating bad PR (to say the least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T10:16:12-07:00","id":1513208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513201#post1513201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, every artist using a model or depicting a real-life landscape, from the Classic Age onwards, would be &quot;tracing&quot;, then: I don't think there's a lot of artists whose work only come out of their imagination, without prior reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is interpreting things in your own style and there is copy pasting something and adding a filter mask to it. Thus you're conflating two very different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T10:16:47-07:00","id":1513209,"title":"","content":"There's also the fact that we're talking about the cover of a book that's likely to be around fifty dollars and if they couldn't be bothered to get some original, non-traced art for the thing that everyone is going to see whether they buy W5 or not, is not a promising sign for the rest of the book and it's art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T10:37:01-07:00","id":1513210,"title":"","content":"I came to this thread with the intention of making a sarcastic remark about how wonderful it was that by the 3rd preview they were able to release more previews without controversy than with. Turns out I greatly over estimated their abilities and professionalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 05-29-2023, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T14:23:10-07:00","id":1513232,"title":"","content":"Yeah...I think I'm just gonna start blocking people that are defending this bullshit, they're basically stating they are fine with theft of IP. Stock Photos are fine to use as reference but at minimum should be acknowledged as the source especially in a commercial product. There are also numerous images involved here that are not stock art and the owners have neither been informed or acknowledged in the use of their images. The artist in question has also gone through their online portfolio and removed any past references to their sources.<br /> <br /> People also keep bringing up the tracing of Dante in the 1st Ed Hunter book like its a gotcha....its not, that artist was reprimanded and blacklisted from further work on OPP books. Others bring up Timothy Bradstreet who did a lot of photo-reference/tracing work in past WW books but he always credited his sources and paid his photo models.<br /> <br /> Based on what we now know and are extremely likely to find in the future defending this artist should be treated the same as defending piracy on this forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T23:51:18-07:00","id":1513267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513232#post1513232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People also keep bringing up the tracing of Dante in the 1st Ed Hunter book like its a gotcha....its not, that artist was reprimanded and blacklisted from further work on OPP books. Others bring up Timothy Bradstreet who did a lot of photo-reference/tracing work in past WW books but he always credited his sources and paid his photo models.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I mean, Bradstreet poses the model, sets the scene and then takes the photo himself. Whether you like his style or not, he is using his own art through the process. Comparing the W5 artist to him is highly flawed and insulting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The artist in question has also gone through their online portfolio and removed any past references to their sources.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Umm, wow. Do you have any proof of this?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T00:35:56-07:00","id":1513270,"title":"","content":"I think we need to differentiate two things here.<br /> <br /> Firstly, the artist is one that uses photos as a baseline to create his art. Their technique is speedpainting/photomanipulation. This is not a problem in itself. If you like it or not it's down to personal preference. Of course they use references since they are the baseline of their artstyle.<br /> <br /> Second, the questional ethics of what the subject matter is the problem here. I am not fussed about obvious stock imagery and we shouldn't be either. The problem is when it's actual people who didn't sign up for it and when the imagery is owned by other artists not credited in the book. There hasn't been a credit like that in the past books, nor has Paradox adressed this concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T00:39:10-07:00","id":1513271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513267#post1513267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Umm, wow. Do you have any proof of this?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a <a href=\"https://twitter.com/TheCyberRecord/status/1663080955731652608\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter-thread </a>from TheCyberRecord. After the GW-debacle the artist deleted his instagram-account so a lot has been lost but what that Twitter-user was able to recover was a particular instagram-post of a drawing for H5 that had been edited. And going further back he found that what had been edited out was a link to a stock-photo-database. So he used to cite his photo-references. Someone else also claimed that recently he had been saying that he actually doesn't use photo-references - but the artist has been pruning his social media after the stuff with the GW-preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T07:05:31-07:00","id":1513288,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's perfectly possible to ethically trace art or reuse likenesses, it's not unbelievable that the delay after the Glass Walkers preview was to make sure that this wasn't the case (although from what I understand highly unlikely given the reference in question). But the replacement of the GW art suggests it isn't the case here, and unfortunately for Paradox Werewolf is the line that's going to be combed over for anything suspicious. As I understand it can be even more complicated legally where a piece of art might be public domain and/or remixable but the likenesses might not be.<br /> <br /> Hopefully the artist turns over a new leaf and either stops tracing or starts tracing ethically. Sadly it's probably too late to save at least the first printing of W5, even if every single piece of their artwork was pulled.<br /> <br /> It might be worth going over the credits after the book is out and seeing if they've provided credits for stock photos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T07:25:02-07:00","id":1513289,"title":"","content":"And the bad news for Paradox is that it isn't only the art-section where the credits will be interesting. We've learned from James Sambrano that they have been reusing bits of text (or names like Ghost Council) from the first iteration of W5, so the question there is if the writers of the first iteration will be credited in this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T18:13:20-07:00","id":1513490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513072#post1513072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly you could do a WtA reboot that didn't focus on the werewolf aspect that much. Go hard on the eco-terrorist/shaman angle, ramp up the importance of playable Kinfolk, and really bang that 'the Garou are dying' drum.<br /> <br /> It would be like making a Star Wars game without playable Jedi, but in the same way it could work. I even personally prefer that side of Werewolf to the raging death monster and tribal meetings side. But of course at that point you might as well call it Kinfolk: the Uprising rather than Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I was toying around with a similarly radical idea of a werewolf game essentially centred around playing as Ronin who have to figure out what being a werewolf means on the own, without the garou nation since they have heavily diminished presence in my setting to the point they seem like an urban myth or a distant ideal than an actual group.<br /> <br /> Also it takes place in project moon's City which is described as Techno Nephandi wet dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T04:30:24-07:00","id":1513520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513490#post1513490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know I was toying around with a similarly radical idea of a werewolf game essentially centred around playing as Ronin who have to figure out what being a werewolf means on the own, without the garou nation since they have heavily diminished presence in my setting to the point they seem like an urban myth or a distant ideal than an actual group.<br /> <br /> Also it takes place in project moon's City which is described as Techno Nephandi wet dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>So generally how I tend to portray the Forsaken in Forsaken? My general rule being that Uratha are few in number and you don't generally find out anything until a pack stumbles across you or you've caused enough disturbance.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course the idea that Garou have never been interacting directly with Gaia and have to figure things out for themselves as W5 seems to run with is interesting, but I'd much rather run it as being more a game of (Googles as commonwealth name is racist) Telephone along the spirit world until you get something humans can kind of grasp than whatever W5 is going with. Figuring out what being a werewolf means can be fun, but it probably shouldn't be the default (goals of playing the game: work out what the game's actually about ...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T14:16:32-07:00","id":1513567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513490#post1513490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know I was toying around with a similarly radical idea of a werewolf game essentially centred around playing as Ronin who have to figure out what being a werewolf means on the own, without the garou nation since they have heavily diminished presence in my setting to the point they seem like an urban myth or a distant ideal than an actual group.<br /> <br /> Also it takes place in project moon's City which is described as Techno Nephandi wet dream.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is quite similar to the thinblood centric v5 and potentially has simular issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T02:59:54-07:00","id":1513623,"title":"","content":"Having multiple modes of play enabled and suggested is fun! M20 empowers you to play a Traditions, Crafts, Technocracy, Orphan or mixed game. V20 empowers you to play Camarilla, Sabbat, TBH, Anarch, clan-specific, mixed, and so on.<br /> <br /> W20 has a few modes of play, but they're largely geographical. Garou. A type of Fera. Mixed Fera. Beast Courts. Ahadi. Ancient times. There's options! But having more content to look at a Ronin game, or a mixed game, would be cool. It should just be something which is facilitated without consuming the core of the game.<br /> <br /> W5 feels like it's built to be played one specific way - you're a too cool for school pack who work at street level and get a Caern, and mostly do human stuff, with some fights, without ever building anything big or collaborationist as other Garou are bad, and big groups make trouble. Unless changes have been made from the glimpses and hints we got, which is more than possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T17:44:35-07:00","id":1513831,"title":"","content":"Another query. If all Tribe members are restricted by the Patrons ban, presumably there is also a ban from your Caern and Pack Patrons....does this mean all beginning Garou essentially start with 3 levels of Chiminage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T17:59:45-07:00","id":1513834,"title":"","content":"I don't think we have nearly enough information to answer that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T04:29:09-07:00","id":1513858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1513623#post1513623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having multiple modes of play enabled and suggested is fun! M20 empowers you to play a Traditions, Crafts, Technocracy, Orphan or mixed game. V20 empowers you to play Camarilla, Sabbat, TBH, Anarch, clan-specific, mixed, and so on.<br /> <br /> W20 has a few modes of play, but they're largely geographical. Garou. A type of Fera. Mixed Fera. Beast Courts. Ahadi. Ancient times. There's options! But having more content to look at a Ronin game, or a mixed game, would be cool. It should just be something which is facilitated without consuming the core of the game.<br /> <br /> W5 feels like it's built to be played one specific way - you're a too cool for school pack who work at street level and get a Caern, and mostly do human stuff, with some fights, without ever building anything big or collaborationist as other Garou are bad, and big groups make trouble. Unless changes have been made from the glimpses and hints we got, which is more than possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>W5 follow the trend of 5th edition.<br /> <br /> V5 is built around street level anarch play, H5 forbid you from going above a cell of hunters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T05:37:31-07:00","id":1513863,"title":"","content":"While I think everyone understands that's going to be the case, the issue is more how that's going to impact what W5 really looks like compared to WtA's past.<br /> <br /> VtM, and even the various types of hunters, have always had play styles that roughly correlate to the power levels of the characters. Relatively young vampires of any Sect largely have similar play styles because what concerns their immediate survive and ability to secure a more viable long term existence is more about the basic kindred condition than organizational dogma. Vampires need to hit certain rungs of power before they can really hold their own in the cutthroat politics of the Camarilla, navigate the complex web of individual personalities of the Anarchs, or be someone that gives orders in the militant Sabbat. Lke-wise, there's always been &quot;cell&quot; level hunters, and if you wanted to move past that you grabbed the books for playing &quot;org&quot; hunters (and whatever the Imbued would count as if they were part of H5).<br /> <br /> Werewolf, (and Mage, and Changeling as well) start to decouple that assumption quickly. Even in WtA 1e, the default assumption was more that the PCs would be mobile, as older PCs are the ones that settled down at one Caern to be high ranking Sept officers. PCs would make use of Moon Bridges to travel rapidly and relatively reliably around the world to the kinds of conflicts they were built by the players to get into, while searching for a place to put down roots as they gain Rank and duties along with it. You didn't have to play globetrotting games by any means, but there weren't the barriers stopping young Garou from doing that like there were and are for vampires and hunters.<br /> <br /> Adding those roadblocks to keep Garou tied down to one place to keep to that one core supported game play style is going to radically alter what Werewolf in a fashion I think even the &quot;reboot, not continuation&quot; pitch is really going to manage to cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T05:59:44-07:00","id":1513867,"title":"","content":"We already saw some hints with the latest preview in the Finishing Touches section. It's an indication to some degree of what the game's relationship with &quot;being a Garou&quot; is when the questions it suggests you should talk about with your players are this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One very important thing to bear in mind about your character is how they view being Garou. How do they feel about living through an ongoing Apocalypse? Do they believe it\u2019s the Apocalypse at all, or is that doomer nihilism? Do they know other werewolves, and if so, how do they relate to them? Or is their pack isolated, and does their sense of \u201cGarou culture\u201d begin and end with the pack?\u200b </div> </div> </div>The narrative dial this is going for isn't to suggest different options for what the character's relationship to being a Garou is but rather &quot;How much of Garou-culture/tradition/worldview do you want to include/exclude?&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the next paragraph with its first sentence sounds like it's going for the same idea:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they care a great deal for their tribe and how it affects their sense of self? Or is the Patron Spirit an aloof\u200b... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T22:22:36-07:00","id":1514162,"title":"","content":"No sight of a preview yet, so either there is some art restructuring going on or they decided not to feed the criticism fire more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T00:20:06-07:00","id":1514171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1514162#post1514162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No sight of a preview yet, so either there is some art restructuring going on or they decided not to feed the criticism fire more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either there are no more previews coming or maybe they're waiting for the Renegade-hosted stream (about the WOD) this weekend to reveal more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T01:27:46-07:00","id":1514174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1514171#post1514171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Either there are no more previews coming or maybe they're waiting for the Renegade-hosted stream (about the WOD) this weekend to reveal more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T05:50:46-07:00","id":1514187,"title":"","content":"Does WoD still do their weekly news stream on Twitch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T06:00:45-07:00","id":1514190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512578-ghost-council-tribe-preview-for-w5?p=1514187#post1514187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does WoD still do their weekly news stream on Twitch?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the new one happens in two hours. The thing is the only time Outstar provided more detailed commentary was when the first couple of pages of the preview had been released. In the next two shows after that, she only very briefly talked about the previews. And then she went on holiday, so her last show was 3 weeks ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T06:16:44-07:00","id":1514192,"title":"","content":"If they are going to delay it due to art concerns, it would be a positive mark on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T08:24:38-07:00","id":1514197,"title":"","content":"Been watching it and so far nothing regarding the art or any talk of a delay. So doubtful anything regarding that will happen.<br /> <br /> Other than that, it has been announced that the previews of this week will be part of the Renegade-streams and the focus will be on W5 character-creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}